3194139535716 true] [17592186363024 1113 #uuid "a3bb3ced-7db7-5b87-94c1-62537aeec042" 13194139535716 true] [17592186363024 1145 "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{2x-5} & =50\\cdot {3}^{2x-5} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{2x-5}-50\\cdot {3}^{2x-5} & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}-50)\\cdot {3}^{2x-5} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-50=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{3}^{2x-5}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $2{x}^{2}-50=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}^{2}-25) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+5)(x-5) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-5,5.$\n\n- The equation $2=0$ is not a possible solution because it's a false statement.\n\n- The equation ${3}^{2x-5}=0$ has no solutions because ${3}^{2x-5}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-5\\,\\text{and}\\,x=5.\n$$" 13194139535716 true] [17592186363025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363026 13194139535716 true] [17592186363025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363027 13194139535716 true] [17592186363025 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535716 true] [17592186363025 1041 "field-1" 13194139535716 true] [17592186363025 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363026 13194139535716 true] [17592186363025 1110 #uuid "6b4874eb-da20-5fbe-98e8-a7d3cc21e86a" 13194139535716 true] [17592186363026 1034 "-5" 13194139535716 true] [17592186363026 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535716 true] [17592186363026 1111 #uuid "0a47b2ec-48db-586c-83c7-6986d749de3e" 13194139535716 true] [17592186363027 1034 "-4" 13194139535716 true] [17592186363027 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535716 true] [17592186363027 1111 #uuid "3e596de6-42b8-5a22-a832-311c3c37b97a" 13194139535716 true] [17592186363028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363029 13194139535716 true] [17592186363028 1040 #edb/ref 1759218604